it's?

22
00:02:25,957 --> 00:02:55,937
To be continued...

23
00:02:55,957 --> 00:02:59,277
I'm sorry.

24
00:02:59,397 --> 00:03:01,357
Hey, it's perfectly fine.

25
00:03:01,597 --> 00:03:02,037
Atsiya!

26
00:03:02,657 --> 00:03:04,397
Jeez, where have you been?

27
00:03:05,237 --> 00:03:06,157
Hey there, Sinai.

28
00:03:08,617 --> 00:03:09,137
Wow.

29
00:03:09,657 --> 00:03:11,277
They're perfect for each other.

30
00:03:14,817 --> 00:03:17,177
Sorry, I'm not familiar with the area.

31
00:03:17,837 --> 00:03:18,937
You're bad at directions.

32
00:03:19,417 --> 00:03:19,977
I remember.

33
00:03:20,817 --> 00:03:24,417
You didn't have to come to the next town over just to take this summer course.

34
00:03:24,417 --> 00:03:26,257
But this is where you are.

35
00:03:27,777 --> 00:03:28,577
Ah, damn.

36
00:03:29,297 --> 00:03:30,257
Our eyes just met.

37
00:03:30,697 --> 00:03:31,137
Stop.

38
00:03:31,737 --> 00:03:34,557
Hey, you always keep your hair so long, don't you?

39
00:03:35,197 --> 00:03:35,737
How come?

40
00:03:38,297 --> 00:03:40,277
Sinai has become even more beautiful.

41
00:03:40,277 --> 00:03:45,097
I reconnected with her at our relative's funeral.

42
00:03:45,597 --> 00:03:47,277
I hadn't seen her in six years.

43
00:03:49,677 --> 00:03:52,517
She wasn't like any of the other girls in my class.

44
00:03:53,417 --> 00:03:55,857
I don't have any siblings or very many friends.

45
00:03:56,737 --> 00:03:58,097
She's really my only cousin.

46
00:03:58,097 --> 00:04:00,917
What?

47
00:04:01,857 --> 00:04:02,977
Atsiya Kirishima?

48
00:04:03,617 --> 00:04:04,317
That's me.

49
00:04:05,597 --> 00:04:06,677
Oh, damn it.

50
00:04:06,977 --> 00:04:08,397
She's looking at me right now.

51
00:04:08,757 --> 00:04:09,097
You're...

52
00:04:09,617 --> 00:04:11,077
You're huge!

53
00:04:11,457 --> 00:04:12,577
That's insane!

54
00:04:12,677 --> 00:04:14,197
You used to be like this small!

55
00:04:14,597 --> 00:04:15,657
Man, you've grown!

56
00:04:17,317 --> 00:04:17,757
She...

57
00:04:17,757 --> 00:04:19,297
She remembered me.

58
00:04:20,517 --> 00:04:21,717
Sinai...

59
00:04:21,717 --> 00:04:23,037
You've grown a lot, too.

60
00:04:23,897 --> 00:04:24,397
Impressive.

61
00:04:25,077 --> 00:04:25,537
Really?

62
00:04:25,937 --> 00:04:27,377
I haven't changed at all.

63
00:04:28,057 --> 00:04:30,757
You're beautiful.

64
00:04:31,377 --> 00:04:31,937
Let's date.

65
00:04:36,417 --> 00:04:39,237
Sinai couldn't have looked more disgusted with what I said.

66
00:04:39,237 --> 00:04:43,297
Right.

67
00:04:43,937 --> 00:04:44,757
Flashback over.

68
00:04:47,417 --> 00:04:49,257
Sinai has become even more beautiful.

69
00:04:50,357 --> 00:04:51,977
Are you going to become an actress?

70
00:04:52,517 --> 00:04:52,837
What?

71
00:04:53,137 --> 00:04:53,477
No.

72
00:04:53,797 --> 00:04:55,237
I plan on going to college.

73
00:04:58,897 --> 00:05:00,237
I'm persistent with her.

74
00:05:01,097 --> 00:05:02,177
I don't give up.

75
00:05:02,877 --> 00:05:05,177
I know Sinai has a crush that's too much for her.

76
00:05:06,097 --> 00:05:07,277
I just don't care.

77
00:05:09,237 --> 00:05:12,177
So then you're telling me you have a crush from your high school?

78
00:05:12,877 --> 00:05:13,717
That's fine, then.

79
00:05:14,177 --> 00:05:14,817
Why is that?

80
00:05:15,397 --> 00:05:17,497
I mean, that's not the only crush you'll ever have.

81
00:05:18,137 --> 00:05:21,357
And besides, it doesn't seem like it's going to work out anyway.

82
00:05:22,277 --> 00:05:24,997
I can tell by the way you've been moping around here lately.

83
00:05:27,277 --> 00:05:29,917
I'm just another helpful and concerned friend.

84
00:05:30,517 --> 00:05:31,957
And a male relative to Boot.

85
00:05:32,817 --> 00:05:35,877
That's why I want to know everything about Sinai.

86
00:05:36,377 --> 00:05:37,417
Who I like.

87
00:05:38,277 --> 00:05:39,097
It's a girl.

88
00:05:39,237 --> 00:05:42,617
Understand?

89
00:05:43,617 --> 00:05:45,457
I'll never have feelings for you.

90
00:05:47,397 --> 00:05:47,877
Sinai.

91
00:05:49,397 --> 00:05:51,797
Do you really like her because she's actually a girl?

92
00:05:52,957 --> 00:05:54,857
And it's not working out because of that?

93
00:05:57,697 --> 00:05:59,237
Oh, I'm sorry.

94
00:06:00,397 --> 00:06:02,397
I'm not very good with complicated issues.

95
00:06:02,397 --> 00:06:04,257
Maybe I'm insensitive.

96
00:06:04,857 --> 00:06:07,317
So, let's see.

97
00:06:07,717 --> 00:06:10,377
This is the first time you've actually fallen in love with someone.

98
00:06:10,977 --> 00:06:12,397
Well, that makes me happy for you.

99
00:06:12,797 --> 00:06:15,717
And if you like her so much, then I do too.

100
00:06:16,777 --> 00:06:17,217
Okay?

101
00:06:17,217 --> 00:06:21,597
Don't you see?

102
00:06:21,597 --> 00:06:24,757
I probably hate all guys.

103
00:06:24,757 --> 00:06:27,317
But you really don't hate me, do you?

104
00:06:28,977 --> 00:06:34,017
Which means then, you're looking at me as the individual person, Atsuya Kirishima.

105
00:06:34,017 --> 00:06:39,177
Basically, gender doesn't really come into any play between us.

106
00:06:39,397 --> 00:06:40,237
Yeah, but look.

107
00:06:40,397 --> 00:06:42,437
I don't need to put any gender labels on you.

108
00:06:43,157 --> 00:06:43,917
You're my cousin.

109
00:06:44,597 --> 00:06:47,377
Yes, but do you like her because you've given her a label to wear?

110
00:06:47,817 --> 00:06:48,297
No.

111
00:06:48,297 --> 00:06:51,797
Well, then that still means I have a chance with you.

112
00:06:54,597 --> 00:06:55,077
Damn.

113
00:06:55,577 --> 00:06:56,297
Our eyes met.

114
00:07:01,117 --> 00:07:02,137
Did I study?

115
00:07:02,957 --> 00:07:04,037
Of course I did.

116
00:07:05,477 --> 00:07:05,917
Technically.

117
00:07:07,597 --> 00:07:09,257
We're both serious students.

118
00:07:10,457 --> 00:07:12,337
And we're both in the honor program.

119
00:07:18,297 --> 00:07:19,937
You scared?

120
00:07:20,697 --> 00:07:21,117
Yeah.

121
00:07:21,697 --> 00:07:23,197
I'm like...

122
00:07:23,197 --> 00:07:24,357
Really terrified.

123
00:07:25,497 --> 00:07:27,137
I don't want to hear her answer.

124
00:07:27,837 --> 00:07:28,817
Though I know it's a no.

125
00:07:32,497 --> 00:07:34,757
You can pretend I'm her if you'd like to.

126
00:07:37,637 --> 00:07:38,797
What the...

127
00:07:38,797 --> 00:07:40,037
Why did I mention that?

128
00:07:40,537 --> 00:07:41,657
What's gotten into me?

129
00:07:42,077 --> 00:07:43,737
There's no reason to say that.

130
00:07:44,377 --> 00:07:45,917
That was our original arrangement.

131
00:07:46,717 --> 00:07:47,437
After all.

132
00:07:48,697 --> 00:07:49,217
Pretend?

133
00:07:49,837 --> 00:07:50,537
Just me?

134
00:07:54,697 --> 00:07:55,417
It's okay.

135
00:07:56,037 --> 00:07:56,757
It's fine.

136
00:07:57,537 --> 00:07:57,937
What?

137
00:07:58,077 --> 00:07:59,657
I don't get what you're saying right now.

138
00:08:00,737 --> 00:08:01,357
Tell me.

139
00:08:01,577 --> 00:08:03,157
I won't know if you don't say something.

140
00:08:03,697 --> 00:08:05,457
Maybe we...

141
00:08:05,457 --> 00:08:08,417
Maybe he's feeling the same thing.

142
00:08:09,277 --> 00:08:10,417
It's just...

143
00:08:10,417 --> 00:08:11,677
I don't know when it started.

144
00:08:12,617 --> 00:08:14,197
But lately it seems...

145
00:08:14,197 --> 00:08:15,677
I can't imagine you as her.

146
00:08:15,677 --> 00:08:17,817
Does that mean...

147
00:08:17,817 --> 00:08:18,317
He possibly...

148
00:08:18,317 --> 00:08:19,917
Oh God.

149
00:08:20,337 --> 00:08:22,517
I don't know what to say about any of that.

150
00:08:23,237 --> 00:08:23,757
Why?

151
00:08:24,357 --> 00:08:24,917
Come on.

152
00:08:25,457 --> 00:08:27,437
I need to say something to him.

153
00:08:29,917 --> 00:08:30,837
Well...

154
00:08:30,837 --> 00:08:31,637
I guess.

155
00:08:32,457 --> 00:08:34,357
We've both decided we're gonna do this.

156
00:08:34,877 --> 00:08:36,117
We'll just have to see what happens.

157
00:08:36,117 --> 00:08:45,737
And that was it.

158
00:08:46,257 --> 00:08:47,577
That was when I realized.

159
00:08:48,857 --> 00:08:50,117
It was different.

160
00:08:50,957 --> 00:08:54,057
And I had also stopped comparing Mugi with brother like that.

161
00:08:54,857 --> 00:08:56,397
I regarded them separately.

162
00:08:56,397 --> 00:09:01,617
This is far enough.

163
00:09:02,297 --> 00:09:02,977
I'm good now.

164
00:09:03,417 --> 00:09:04,337
Thanks for walking me.

165
00:09:04,337 --> 00:09:05,257
Hmm.

166
00:09:22,257 --> 00:09:24,397
Summer is so short.

167
00:09:24,397 --> 00:09:41,677
And we can't rewind time.

168
00:09:41,677 --> 00:09:43,937
We'll be right back.

169
00:09:44,377 --> 00:09:44,437
But...

170
00:09:44,437 --> 00:10:00,557
We'll be right back.

171
00:10:00,557 --> 00:10:18,757
Brother!

172
00:10:19,317 --> 00:10:19,677
Huh?

173
00:10:21,957 --> 00:10:23,677
When did you start wearing glasses?

174
00:10:24,317 --> 00:10:25,677
Well, do I look good in them?

175
00:10:26,157 --> 00:10:26,477
Yeah.

176
00:10:27,057 --> 00:10:28,597
It makes you look like a real teacher.

177
00:10:29,177 --> 00:10:29,697
Congrats.

178
00:10:29,697 --> 00:10:30,877
On your exam.

179
00:10:31,637 --> 00:10:32,577
Yeah, you too.

180
00:10:33,257 --> 00:10:36,177
Thanks, but mine was just a silly high school entrance exam.

181
00:10:37,217 --> 00:10:38,937
That's still no easy feat.

182
00:10:39,597 --> 00:10:41,757
Yeah, but you realized what your dream was.

183
00:10:42,057 --> 00:10:42,877
That's great.

184
00:10:43,257 --> 00:10:44,757
You're a certified teacher now.

185
00:10:47,817 --> 00:10:48,377
What?

186
00:10:49,097 --> 00:10:49,617
Seriously?

187
00:10:49,837 --> 00:10:50,797
You're crying now?

188
00:10:50,977 --> 00:10:54,297
I mean, it made me realize how much you've grown up.

189
00:10:54,577 --> 00:10:55,177
You know that?

190
00:10:55,317 --> 00:10:58,217
Man, there you go treating me like a kid again.

191
00:10:58,217 --> 00:11:01,097
Oh, what?

192
00:11:01,097 --> 00:11:02,777
Hey, you remember?

193
00:11:03,497 --> 00:11:05,677
The time you got lost on that big snow day?

194
00:11:06,277 --> 00:11:08,557
We walked home, holding hands together.

195
00:11:09,437 --> 00:11:11,777
Yeah, but that seems like a long time ago.

196
00:11:12,137 --> 00:11:12,957
Oh, come on.

197
00:11:13,157 --> 00:11:13,737
Just a day.

198
00:11:14,257 --> 00:11:15,017
Just to your house.

199
00:11:16,157 --> 00:11:16,597
What?

200
00:11:16,957 --> 00:11:18,197
That's too embarrassing.

201
00:11:18,197 --> 00:11:25,077
I have so many fond memories.

202
00:11:26,277 --> 00:11:27,897
Most of them are so trivial.

203
00:11:29,217 --> 00:11:30,777
But precious memories to me.

204
00:11:31,457 --> 00:11:33,097
I'll treasure them all my life.

205
00:11:35,057 --> 00:11:36,557
Have you remembered any of them?

206
00:11:37,537 --> 00:11:38,957
The sheer thought of that happening?

207
00:11:38,957 --> 00:11:41,957
That means I can go on living.

208
00:11:42,437 --> 00:11:44,597
I'm not exaggerating in the least about that.

209
00:11:46,517 --> 00:11:48,257
There's nobody better than you.

210
00:11:49,337 --> 00:11:51,197
And the whole entire world.

211
00:11:51,197 --> 00:12:06,377
No matter how warped or clumsy it was,

212
00:12:07,157 --> 00:12:10,077
I have loved as hard as I can.

213
00:12:10,077 --> 00:12:23,137
No, I won't run anymore.

214
00:12:28,137 --> 00:12:28,737
Finally.

215
00:12:29,497 --> 00:12:30,557
Homework is done.

216
00:12:31,357 --> 00:12:31,657
Hmm.

217
00:12:32,017 --> 00:12:33,537
You'll do it tomorrow afternoon?

218
00:12:34,137 --> 00:12:35,177
I'll go at night then.

219
00:12:35,877 --> 00:12:37,017
Let's confess it all.

220
00:12:37,817 --> 00:12:38,977
You mean get rejected?

221
00:12:38,977 --> 00:12:41,657
Sorry, I didn't mean it.

222
00:12:42,617 --> 00:12:44,077
But this is good.

223
00:12:44,737 --> 00:12:45,537
Not being alone.

224
00:12:46,097 --> 00:12:46,917
We'll fail together.

225
00:12:47,737 --> 00:12:48,037
Hmm.

226
00:12:48,357 --> 00:12:48,937
You're right.

227
00:12:49,537 --> 00:12:50,597
Well, alright.

228
00:12:51,017 --> 00:12:52,337
Let's meet back here tomorrow.

229
00:12:52,797 --> 00:12:53,777
Say around 10pm.

230
00:12:55,397 --> 00:12:55,917
Hmm.

231
00:12:57,437 --> 00:12:58,497
This is hard.

232
00:12:59,177 --> 00:13:01,677
I can't seem to look at Mookie's face directly.

233
00:13:02,957 --> 00:13:04,637
Why is this happening now?

234
00:13:06,277 --> 00:13:08,497
Well, I'll see you.

235
00:13:09,577 --> 00:13:10,897
Oh, God.

236
00:13:11,277 --> 00:13:11,757
Seriously?

237
00:13:12,437 --> 00:13:13,397
What is this?

238
00:13:14,197 --> 00:13:15,537
My face feels warm.

239
00:13:20,537 --> 00:13:21,157
Good night.

240
00:13:21,157 --> 00:13:25,117
What the hell?

241
00:13:25,117 --> 00:13:28,017
Was that his way of cheering me on?

242
00:13:28,937 --> 00:13:30,617
But I guess...

243
00:13:30,617 --> 00:13:32,717
All this excitement...

244
00:13:32,717 --> 00:13:34,937
Helps stop my shaking, at least.

245
00:13:35,977 --> 00:13:38,277
I feel weird getting excited with Mookie.

246
00:13:40,557 --> 00:13:41,157
But...

247
00:13:41,157 --> 00:13:42,577
I don't hate it.

248
00:13:42,577 --> 00:13:43,117
Maybe...

249
00:13:43,117 --> 00:13:49,377
I can move forward after all.

250
00:13:49,377 --> 00:13:49,417
I can move forward after all.

251
00:13:49,417 --> 00:14:02,657
That was strange.

252
00:14:02,877 --> 00:14:04,537
I had a dream about holding hands.

253
00:14:04,537 --> 00:14:09,177
I wonder who it was with.

254
00:14:11,497 --> 00:14:12,557
Hey there, Mookie.

255
00:14:13,217 --> 00:14:14,337
Well, what's going on?

256
00:14:14,557 --> 00:14:15,997
It's a little hot today, huh?

257
00:14:16,437 --> 00:14:16,917
You're right.

258
00:14:17,457 --> 00:14:18,117
I'm sorry.

259
00:14:18,717 --> 00:14:20,277
Thanks for coming here to meet me.

260
00:14:20,737 --> 00:14:21,457
It's fine.

261
00:14:21,657 --> 00:14:23,697
I'll do anything for my dear sweet student.

262
00:14:24,697 --> 00:14:26,597
Besides, you're one of the special ones.

263
00:14:27,257 --> 00:14:28,737
You need advice about your future?

264
00:14:28,737 --> 00:14:31,397
Well, here I go.

265
00:14:32,377 --> 00:14:34,037
I'm about to get rejected by her.

266
00:14:35,717 --> 00:14:37,437
She still keeps it up, doesn't she?

267
00:14:38,477 --> 00:14:39,617
That mask of hers.

268
00:14:40,797 --> 00:14:41,537
Not that.

269
00:14:42,597 --> 00:14:43,717
Well, you see, I...

270
00:14:43,717 --> 00:14:43,857
Huh?

271
00:14:44,377 --> 00:14:45,377
Well, what is it then?

272
00:14:45,737 --> 00:14:45,977
Huh?

273
00:14:46,657 --> 00:14:47,457
Uh...

274
00:14:47,457 --> 00:14:50,137
I'm getting a bit thirsty out here.

275
00:14:50,817 --> 00:14:51,777
Let's go to a cafe.

276
00:14:55,737 --> 00:14:57,477
It seems I've let her take the lead.

277
00:14:58,737 --> 00:15:01,937
Did you get a tan, Mookie?

278
00:15:02,457 --> 00:15:02,757
Huh?

279
00:15:03,037 --> 00:15:03,737
You think?

280
00:15:04,397 --> 00:15:05,317
That's terrific.

281
00:15:06,017 --> 00:15:08,297
I was really worried I wouldn't get a tan.

282
00:15:09,857 --> 00:15:12,017
That's almost hurtful in a strange way.

283
00:15:12,337 --> 00:15:14,337
There's nothing wrong with being pale and white.

284
00:15:14,637 --> 00:15:15,997
It has its appeal as well.

285
00:15:16,257 --> 00:15:16,757
Oh, no.

286
00:15:17,017 --> 00:15:18,857
It's more than a little pale in my case.

287
00:15:18,997 --> 00:15:20,597
I'm like a walking corpse in daylight.

288
00:15:21,117 --> 00:15:21,937
Is that so?

289
00:15:22,457 --> 00:15:24,157
I wouldn't be too harsh about it.

290
00:15:24,157 --> 00:15:25,677
I think girls prefer that.

291
00:15:27,037 --> 00:15:27,717
Is she for real?

292
00:15:27,717 --> 00:15:29,597
Does she like pop idols?

293
00:15:30,137 --> 00:15:31,737
Or is she more of a jock groupie?

294
00:15:32,537 --> 00:15:33,957
She must like the pretty ones.

295
00:15:34,657 --> 00:15:36,677
Though she did sleep with some old bald dude.

296
00:15:40,517 --> 00:15:41,717
So then...

297
00:15:42,257 --> 00:15:43,737
What about me?

298
00:15:46,257 --> 00:15:47,717
Miss Minagawa...

299
00:15:47,717 --> 00:15:50,137
I love you.

300
00:15:50,137 --> 00:16:00,217
Or I used to.

301
00:16:00,897 --> 00:16:01,817
Well, I knew that.

302
00:16:03,057 --> 00:16:04,397
I knew you knew that.

303
00:16:04,977 --> 00:16:06,397
Well, that part I didn't know about.

304
00:16:08,537 --> 00:16:09,537
But you're a liar.

305
00:16:09,537 --> 00:16:12,477
Look, I like you, Mugi.

306
00:16:13,197 --> 00:16:13,777
I do.

307
00:16:15,777 --> 00:16:16,877
Don't get excited.

308
00:16:18,117 --> 00:16:20,297
I know that you're always lying to people.

309
00:16:20,797 --> 00:16:21,797
That's not relative.

310
00:16:22,797 --> 00:16:23,237
I know.

311
00:16:24,297 --> 00:16:25,497
Because I've watched you.

312
00:16:26,917 --> 00:16:27,357
Hey.

313
00:16:27,737 --> 00:16:28,697
What are you doing?

314
00:16:29,977 --> 00:16:31,037
Pull back already.

315
00:16:31,037 --> 00:16:33,257
Don't do this.

316
00:16:33,397 --> 00:16:34,417
Stop being an idiot.

317
00:16:35,457 --> 00:16:36,037
She's someone...

318
00:16:37,497 --> 00:16:38,037
I can...

319
00:16:38,817 --> 00:16:39,437
Never have.

320
00:16:42,197 --> 00:16:43,277
That's why I liked her.

321
00:16:44,557 --> 00:16:46,137
She wasn't obtainable.

322
00:16:46,497 --> 00:16:47,497
I couldn't have her.

323
00:16:48,777 --> 00:16:49,417
Then...

324
00:16:49,417 --> 00:16:50,037
What about...

325
00:16:51,077 --> 00:16:51,797
That's why.

326
00:16:52,037 --> 00:16:53,037
I know there's no way...

327
00:16:53,777 --> 00:16:54,877
You care about me.

328
00:16:55,677 --> 00:16:57,377
But she's right in front of me.

329
00:16:58,557 --> 00:16:58,877
Looking...

330
00:16:59,817 --> 00:17:00,457
Right at me.

331
00:17:01,217 --> 00:17:02,377
It's not a lie.

332
00:17:03,197 --> 00:17:04,137
You must have known.

333
00:17:04,497 --> 00:17:06,037
I've always cared about you two.

334
00:17:07,557 --> 00:17:09,237
But I'd already...

335
00:17:09,237 --> 00:17:09,877
Decided...

336
00:17:10,577 --> 00:17:12,857
I would never leave her alone again.

337
00:17:16,897 --> 00:17:17,877
For the record...

338
00:17:18,497 --> 00:17:19,237
I do know.

339
00:17:19,877 --> 00:17:20,137
Huh?

340
00:17:20,777 --> 00:17:21,837
And what is that?

341
00:17:22,177 --> 00:17:23,357
What you really are!

342
00:17:23,357 --> 00:17:26,057
That you're a horrible, promiscuous, broken narcissist.

343
00:17:26,757 --> 00:17:27,677
And no matter what...

344
00:17:27,677 --> 00:17:29,157
You'll never fall in love with anyone.

345
00:17:29,957 --> 00:17:32,057
But that your men must follow different rules.

346
00:17:32,137 --> 00:17:34,157
Because you're not satisfied unless you are loved.

347
00:17:34,757 --> 00:17:35,437
But...

348
00:17:35,437 --> 00:17:37,277
Even my feelings for you...

349
00:17:37,277 --> 00:17:37,897
Don't matter.

350
00:17:38,557 --> 00:17:39,357
Because really...

351
00:17:40,037 --> 00:17:41,417
It doesn't have to be me.

352
00:17:42,597 --> 00:17:43,837
You're so cute.

353
00:17:45,077 --> 00:17:47,837
Then why bother following me all the way here?

354
00:17:48,617 --> 00:17:48,977
Yeah.

355
00:17:49,497 --> 00:17:51,737
I know this is my own dumbass fault.

356
00:17:53,357 --> 00:17:56,877
It's like an NPC villager confronting the final boss.

357
00:17:57,757 --> 00:17:58,797
I'll admit that.

358
00:18:00,077 --> 00:18:01,677
Because I know...

359
00:18:01,677 --> 00:18:03,217
You'll never care for me.

360
00:18:03,717 --> 00:18:05,177
I'm aware of this imbalance.

361
00:18:05,857 --> 00:18:06,617
She has it all.

362
00:18:07,157 --> 00:18:10,417
And her paper-thin words and fake acting hold no value for me.

363
00:18:10,757 --> 00:18:11,157
But still...

364
00:18:11,157 --> 00:18:12,677
I'm weak.

365
00:18:13,017 --> 00:18:14,557
And the reason I'm here...

366
00:18:14,557 --> 00:18:16,557
Because maybe...

367
00:18:16,557 --> 00:18:18,677
I might just be here first.

368
00:18:20,677 --> 00:18:21,117
And...

369
00:18:21,117 --> 00:18:22,897
I want to change you.

370
00:18:22,897 --> 00:18:27,857
Hey.

371
00:18:28,417 --> 00:18:28,857
Hanabi.

372
00:18:29,857 --> 00:18:31,037
You've finished already?

373
00:18:31,477 --> 00:18:32,337
All that homework?

374
00:18:33,797 --> 00:18:34,277
Yes.

375
00:18:34,697 --> 00:18:35,097
Teacher.

376
00:18:37,097 --> 00:18:39,757
It feels like I haven't seen you in a while.

377
00:18:40,697 --> 00:18:41,257
Well...

378
00:18:41,257 --> 00:18:44,557
Since we're on summer break, that would until not getting to see you as much.

379
00:18:45,277 --> 00:18:45,557
Huh?

380
00:18:45,557 --> 00:18:48,617
Brother, do you know yet?

381
00:18:49,017 --> 00:18:51,177
Have you figured out the reason why I asked you here?

382
00:18:51,917 --> 00:18:52,397
What?

383
00:18:52,757 --> 00:18:53,237
No.

384
00:18:53,657 --> 00:18:54,217
What is it?

385
00:18:55,397 --> 00:18:56,937
I have no idea why.

386
00:18:58,517 --> 00:19:00,237
I like that most about you.

387
00:19:00,817 --> 00:19:01,217
You know?

388
00:19:01,777 --> 00:19:02,637
Hey now.

389
00:19:02,837 --> 00:19:03,737
You're making fun.

390
00:19:04,277 --> 00:19:05,377
I used to like you.

391
00:19:05,497 --> 00:19:06,317
But not anymore?

392
00:19:06,877 --> 00:19:07,657
That's a lie.

393
00:19:07,657 --> 00:19:09,537
I still like you.

394
00:19:10,037 --> 00:19:10,297
Huh?

395
00:19:10,297 --> 00:19:14,917
That's what I wanted to tell you tonight.

396
00:19:18,677 --> 00:19:19,777
Since when?

397
00:19:20,277 --> 00:19:23,037
Has he really just been so clueless for all this time?

398
00:19:23,597 --> 00:19:27,737
But I love how quickly he takes me seriously after finding out he's great.

399
00:19:28,677 --> 00:19:30,397
I'd say...

400
00:19:30,397 --> 00:19:32,997
For a long, long time now.

401
00:19:34,077 --> 00:19:37,477
And I love how considerate he is of other people's feelings.

402
00:19:37,477 --> 00:19:41,417
The more I put it into words, the more I feel.

403
00:19:42,957 --> 00:19:44,097
I love his voice.

404
00:19:44,677 --> 00:19:45,537
And his face.

405
00:19:46,297 --> 00:19:48,497
I love his gestures and the way he talks.

406
00:19:49,297 --> 00:19:51,977
I love how good he thinks and all of his compassion.

407
00:19:53,137 --> 00:19:54,297
But above all of that,

408
00:19:55,337 --> 00:19:57,077
I love how you just accept me.

409
00:19:58,117 --> 00:19:59,377
When it's truly important.

410
00:20:01,237 --> 00:20:01,757
Hannah.

411
00:20:01,757 --> 00:20:05,297
I know.

412
00:20:05,977 --> 00:20:06,637
Don't worry.

413
00:20:07,137 --> 00:20:08,037
I'll be okay.

414
00:20:08,517 --> 00:20:08,957
Promise.

415
00:20:09,657 --> 00:20:12,057
I'm only shaking because I know it's not me.

416
00:20:17,657 --> 00:20:20,637
When was the last time I got to cry this hard before?

417
00:20:21,757 --> 00:20:25,197
When I feel how tightly he holds me with his arms wrapped around me,

418
00:20:25,537 --> 00:20:28,497
it makes me realize that this is the first and last time,

419
00:20:28,877 --> 00:20:30,117
which makes me cry more.

420
00:20:30,117 --> 00:20:32,897
He holds me like he's never going to let go.

421
00:20:33,417 --> 00:20:34,477
He's so good to me.

422
00:20:35,177 --> 00:20:38,137
The fact that he cares about me makes me happy.

423
00:20:38,917 --> 00:20:40,357
Even if it's not romantic.

424
00:20:42,397 --> 00:20:45,117
And so my long-lasting, unrequited love...

425
00:20:46,957 --> 00:20:47,357
Hannah.

426
00:20:48,277 --> 00:20:49,057
Thank you.

427
00:20:50,477 --> 00:20:50,997
Ended.

428
00:20:50,997 --> 00:20:56,337
It's okay.

429
00:20:59,337 --> 00:21:00,397
It'll be okay.

430
00:21:04,397 --> 00:21:06,397
I know I'll be able to move on now.

431
00:21:08,297 --> 00:21:09,317
I'm sure of it.

432
00:21:10,897 --> 00:21:12,337
I know I can change.

433
00:21:12,337 --> 00:21:16,957
Because I'm not...

434
00:21:18,017 --> 00:21:20,097
Alone.

